+<a id="agentexecute-turn--waterfall"></a>
+
+#### `agent/execute-turn` — waterfall
+
+Execute the whole admitted turn instead of the standard model/tool loop. Return a reason without calling next() to own all steps, requests, retry, tools, stopping policy and transcript admission. Calling next() delegates without consuming additional input. The host still owns turn boundaries, cancellation, status, queued follow-ups and teardown. No standard step, request or turn-stopping listener runs for a handled turn.
+
+```ts cordis-catalog
+/**
+ * Execute the whole admitted turn instead of the standard model/tool loop.
+ * Return a reason without calling next() to own all steps, requests, retry,
+ * tools, stopping policy and transcript admission. Calling next() delegates
+ * without consuming additional input. The host still owns turn boundaries,
+ * cancellation, status, queued follow-ups and teardown. No standard step,
+ * request or turn-stopping listener runs for a handled turn.
+ * @param payload.agent - the agent whose lifecycle contains the execution.
+ * @param payload.input - initial admitted input and assembled prompt/tools; not yet logged as model input.
+ * @param payload.turn - the open host turn number.
+ * @param payload.signal - cancellation signal; an engine must quiesce before returning.
+ * @param payload.prepareInput - claim next-step input through assembly and pre-step policy.
+ * Call serially with the next step number, only while owning this turn.
+ * The engine logs accepted messages and its own step boundaries before dispatching effects.
+ * Scope-filtered dispatch (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-scope`): agent-scoped listeners receive only that agent.
+ * @mode waterfall
+ */
+'agent/execute-turn'(this: Scoped<Agent>, payload: { agent: Agent; input: Extract<TurnInput, { kind: 'enter' }>; turn: number; signal: AbortSignal; prepareInput: (step: number) => Promise<TurnInput> }, next: () => Promise<TurnExecutionResult>): Promise<TurnExecutionResult>
+```
